\b 9. Current Status\b0\par
The Phase 1 base implementation was committed previously. The responder registration-number, searchable county-selector, and international phone-validation updates are implemented in the working tree but have not been deployed. The system still requires backend deployment, one-time SystemAdmin creation, emulator security-rule tests, and live end-to-end registration testing.\par\par

\b 10. Responder Registration Number Update (2026-09-27)\b0\par
- Added a manually typed, Responder-only Organization Registration Number field with required, length, and allowed-character validation.\par
- Confirmed registration writes the trimmed value only to responder documents; Resident registration omits the field.\par
- Updated Firestore rules to require a 5-to-30-character string at creation and prohibit changes by both responders and SystemAdmins. Existing SystemAdmin verification-field updates remain allowed.\par
- Updated the SystemAdmin dashboard to display pending organizations and their registration numbers for manual KMPDC register checks. The dashboard does not yet provide Verify or Reject actions.\par
- Added README guidance covering the number's source, manual verification, and immutability.\par
- Focused widget tests, Flutter analysis, and Firestore rules dry-run passed. These checks do not replace emulator or live Firebase testing.\par

\b 11. Searchable Service Area County Selector (2026-09-27)\b0\par
- Added dropdown_search 6.0.2 and a separate kenyaCounties constant containing all 47 counties.\par
- Replaced the free-text service-area input with a Responder-only searchable bottom sheet. Search filters the county list, selecting a county updates the field, and the clear button removes the selection.\par
- The required selection flows through RegistrationInput.serviceArea and is trimmed into the responder document. Resident registration does not create a responder document, and location coordinates remain null at registration.\par
- Widget tests verify county list size, Resident visibility, searching for Nairobi using "Nai", selection, clearing, and the required-field error when submitting without a county.\par
- flutter pub get, focused widget tests, flutter analyze, and git diff --check completed successfully. No live Firestore or emulator registration test was run.\par

\b 12. International Phone Number Validation (2026-09-27)\b0\par
- Replaced the fixed Kenya-only phone field with intl_phone_number_input 0.7.5, defaulting the selected country to Kenya and permitting other countries.\par
- Added dlibphonenumber 1.1.73 validation: numbers are parsed with the selected ISO region and checked with isValidNumber(). Valid input is formatted as E.164 before being supplied to registration storage.\par
- Changed the Firestore phone rule to require generic E.164 syntax instead of Kenya-only +254 numbers. The rule checks storage format; numbering-plan validity is checked on the client.\par
- Widget tests cover valid and invalid sample numbers for Kenya, the US, and the UK, and verify E.164 output for a Kenyan number. The package classifies UK national input 1234567890 as a valid 01234 pattern, so the invalid UK test uses 0000000000 instead.\par
- The field allows 25 formatted characters so spacing does not truncate valid international input. Focused widget tests and full Flutter analysis passed; Firestore rules compiled in a dry-run. No live-number assignment lookup is available through this validation.\par
